s: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Feb 2026]\nL9: # Title:Floe: Federated Specialization for Real-Time LLM-SLM Inference\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Chunlin Tian , cite6†Kahou Tam , cite7†Yebo Wu , cite8†Shuaihang Zhong , cite9†Li Li , cite10†Nicholas D. Lane , cite11†Chengzhong Xu L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Floe: Federated Specialization for Real-Time LLM-SLM Inference, by Chunlin Tian and 6 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite12†View PDF cite13†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Deploying large language models (LLMs) in real-time systems remains challenging due to their substantial computational demands and privacy concerns. We propose Floe, a hybrid federated learning framework designed for latency-sensitive, resource-constrained environments. Floe combines a cloud-based black-box LLM with lightweight small language models (SLMs) on edge devices to enable low-latency, privacy-preserving inference.\nL17: Personal data and fine-tuning remain on-device, while the cloud LLM contributes general knowledge without exposing proprietary weights. A heterogeneity-aware LoRA adaptation strategy enables efficient edge deployment across diverse hardware, and a logit-level fusion mechanism enables real-time coordination between edge and cloud models. Extensive experiments demonstrate that Floe enhances user privacy and personalization.\nL18: Moreover, it significantly improves model performance and reduces inference latency on edge devices under real-time constraints compared with baseline approaches.\nL19: Comments:  | Accepted by IEEE Transactions on Parallel and Distributed Systems\nL20: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite14†arXiv:2602.14302 [cs.DC]\nL22:    | (or cite15†arXiv:2602.14302v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL23:    | cite16†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.14302†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Chunlin Tian [cite17†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Sun, 15 Feb 2026 20:28:38 UTC (7,787 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled Floe: Federated Specialization for Real-Time LLM-SLM Inference, by Chunlin Tian and 6 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite12†View PDF L36:   * cite13†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite18†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite19†view license†creativecommons.org L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.DC\nL43: \nL44: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L45: \nL46: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2026-02 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite25†cs L51: cite26†cs.LG L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite27†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite28†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite29†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL72: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL75: \nL76: Bibliographic Explorer (cite30†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL77: \nL78: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL79: \nL80: Connected Papers (cite31†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL81: \nL82: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL83: \nL84: Litmaps (cite32†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL85: \nL86: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL87: \nL88: scite Smart Citations (cite33†What are Smart Cit